Sep-30-2026

To upgrade libdrm:

1. Change LIBDRM_VERS in usr/src/common/libdrm/Makefile and
   usr/src/common/libdrm/Makefile.drm, LIBDRM_HASH (SHA-256 of the
   tarball from https://dri.freedesktop.org/libdrm/) in
   usr/src/common/libdrm/Makefile, and ref/dir in
   usr/src/common/libdrm/Check-patches.  If the archive extension
   changes, change LIBDRM_ARCHIVE and the manifest
   usr/src/pkg/manifests/x11-library-libdrm.mf.

2. Rebase the patches in usr/src/common/libdrm/patches: unpack the new
   tarball twice (libdrm-<version> and libdrm-<version>-ref), apply and
   fix the patches in the first copy, then run Check-patches from
   usr/src/common/libdrm (after "mkdir checkpatch") and copy the result
   to patches/.  Drop patches upstream made unnecessary.

3. The patched drm.h, drm_fourcc.h, drm_mode.h, drm_sarea.h and
   i915_drm.h must be identical to the kernel copies in
   usr/src/uts/common/drm; the "check" target of
   usr/src/common/libdrm/Makefile fails otherwise.  Copy the patched
   headers there and make sure the drm and i915 kernel modules still
   build.  Compare the size of every uAPI structure and the value of
   every DRM_IOCTL_* macro between the old and the new headers: a grown
   core structure changes its ioctl number on illumos (see
   README.illumos, "ioctl numbers") and may need an entry in
   usr/src/lib/libdrm/common/sun_ioctl.c.

4. Compare the sources each library builds (the files() lists in the
   meson.build files) with OBJECTS in usr/src/lib/*/Makefile.com, the
   headers upstream installs with HDRS/DRM_HDRS, and new config.set*()
   defines in meson.build with Makefile.drm.  Update the manifests in
   usr/src/pkg/manifests.

5. Build and package as described in README:
	make install
	make package
   and run /opt/drm-tests/amd64/getsundev and drmdevice on a machine
   with a DRM device.
